& [ExplodedIdentity] is the Phase6 decision surface
  + [exploded_uuid] is 8249ec0f-218e-41b3-9043-63e915ab8403
  + [source_snapshot_uuid] is d8d76cba-5a0d-4510-9b86-52faf2332af6
  + [exhaustion_state] is seven_fold_phase_locked_for_storage_selection_only

/ [ContinuationRequest] -(Delineation)> [Inside], [Outside], [Oracle], [Uncertainty]

& [Inside] is the bounded experiment
  + [candidate] is deterministic JSON environment snapshot
  + [candidate] is SQLite environment header plus ordinal package rows
  + [candidate] is redb environment header plus ordinal package values
  + [scale] is 1, 32, and 256 immutable signed packages with one semantic unit each
  + [measure] is serialized bytes, write time, warm reopen and reconstruction distribution, exact query distribution, dependency cost, and operational properties
  + [result] is retain JSON and memory, select one backend, or preserve an unselected pluggable boundary

& [Outside] is not activated
  + [outside] is production schema migration
  + [outside] is database-authorized semantics
  + [outside] is SQL query replacement for SemanticFabric
  + [outside] is concurrent writer service
  + [outside] is terabyte-scale claims
  + [outside] is embeddings, neural routing, model inference, effects, and FPGA

& [DataDesign] is immutable reconstruction
  + [environment_header] is environment_version, now_epoch_seconds, and TrustStore
  + [package_record] is ordinal, package_id, package_digest, and canonical package JSON
  + [reconstruction] is header plus packages ordered by ordinal
  + [integrity] is reconstructed environment digest equal to the source environment digest
  + [authority] is every reconstructed package readmitted by existing cantor_core before query use
  + [query_oracle] is reconstructed response exactly equal to direct source-environment response

& [DecisionLedger] is explicit
  + [correctness_gate] is mandatory and binary
  + [complexity] is dependency count, native-runtime requirement, migration surface, and inspection accessibility
  + [performance] is median and p95 warm load/reconstruction and query times at each scale
  + [space] is physical bytes divided by canonical JSON bytes
  + [selection_threshold] is material measured benefit against an observed requirement, not merely a faster microbenchmark
  + [default] is retain the simplest adequate JSON-plus-memory boundary when no present requirement is unmet

& [SevenFoldTrace] is the SJS explosion
  + [fold_1] is continued work mapped to the next dependency-ready phase
  + [fold_2] is persistence separated from semantic authority and query meaning
  + [fold_3] is current runtime objects mapped to reconstructable physical records
  + [fold_4] is exact digest and response equality made the correctness oracle
  + [fold_5] is three concrete candidates and three structural scales selected
  + [fold_6] is cache, synthetic-corpus, migration, dependency, corruption, and premature-selection faults made explicit
  + [fold_7] is backend adoption locked behind evidence and an observed unmet requirement

& [AcceptanceCriteria] is PD-AC1 through PD-AC8
  + [PD-AC1] is raw continuation source preserved and SJS processed before the experiment
  + [PD-AC2] is all candidates reconstruct exact environments at all scales
  + [PD-AC3] is all reconstructed environments return the exact oracle ProtocolResponse
  + [PD-AC4] is method, machine, versions, iterations, cache limitation, and corpus shape recorded
  + [PD-AC5] is size, write, load median, load p95, and query metrics emitted machine-readably
  + [PD-AC6] is dependency, inspection, transaction, migration, and interoperability costs compared
  + [PD-AC7] is the result selects, defers, or retains a backend with explicit reasons and nonclaims
  + [PD-AC8] is no later architecture becomes active through the persistence decision
